      "hints": [
        "Use B as a point on the line and form the direction BC=OC−OB.",
        "Write r=OB+λBC with a real scalar parameter.",
        "Check the three components and verify that λ=1 reaches C."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Calculate the direction vector $\\vec{BC} = \\vec{OC} - \\vec{OB}$:\n$$\\vec{BC} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 - 1 \\\\ -1 - 3 \\\\ 3 - (-2) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\mathbf{i} - 4\\mathbf{j} + 5\\mathbf{k}$$",
        "Write down the vector equation of line $l$ using base point $B(1, 3, -2)$ and parameter $\\lambda$:\n$$\\mathbf{r} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} + \\lambda\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} \\quad (\\text{or } \\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{i} + 3\\mathbf{j} - 2\\mathbf{k} + \\lambda(\\mathbf{i} - 4\\mathbf{j} + 5\\mathbf{k}), \\; \\lambda \\in \\mathbb{R})$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Vector Equations of Lines": "Derives $\\mathbf{r}=\\mathbf{i}+3\\mathbf{j}-2\\mathbf{k}+\\lambda(\\mathbf{i}-4\\mathbf{j}+5\\mathbf{k})$. The final result is $\\mathbf{r}=\\mathbf{i}+3\\mathbf{j}-2\\mathbf{k}+\\lambda(\\mathbf{i}-4\\mathbf{j}+5\\mathbf{k})$."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
